<title>SINGAPORE: India to sell Feb Madras high aromatic naphtha.</title>
<headline>India to sell Feb Madras high aromatic naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has issued a tender to sell 27,000 tonnes of high aromatic naphtha (HAN) lifting February 3-5 from Madras on the east coast, industry sources said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The tender closes January 16 and is valid until January 17.</p>
<p>IOC's last Madras HAN export cargo, which lifted January 5-7, was sold at $16.65 per tonne below Japanese spot quotes on a free-on-board basis.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
</text>
